   <notesStmt>
    <note type="project" target="#dat1">This is one of several manuscripts of the poem published as "A Twilight Song," which Whitman sent to <hi rend="italic">The Century Magazine</hi> sometime before February 26, 1890 (See <hi rend="italic">With Walt Whitman in Camden</hi> [Southern Illinois University Press, 1982], <ref target="med.00006.164">6:311</ref>). A seemingly earlier manuscript that contributed to the poem (<ref target="uva.00005">uva.00005</ref>) is written on the reverse of a cancelled draft of the "Note at End," which Whitman wrote in November 1888 for <hi rend="italic">Complete Poems and Prose</hi>. The present manuscript, then, must have been written sometime between late 1888 and early 1890.</note>
    
     <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00398" cert="high">Manuscript draft of "A Twilight Song," which was first published in the May 1890 issue of <hi rend="italic">The Century Illustrated Monthly Magazine</hi>. Whitman included the poem, with slight revisions, in <hi rend="italic">Good-Bye My Fancy</hi> (1891).
     </note>
   </notesStmt>
   
